'''Line A''' of the [[CristoCarril]] (CC) system is a commuter rail line operated by [[Intercon]] that runs on the [[Coastal Line]] corridor between [[Barcelona Main Station]] in [[Sant Cristòfor]] and the [[Estació Central de Portnou]] in [[Portnou]]. The line is the longest CristoCarril route, covering 83.3 km and serving 16 stations across three comarcas — [[Sant Cristòfor (comarca)|Sant Cristòfor]], [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará]], and [[Marjal del Canal (comarca)|Marjal del Canal]] — before terminating at Portnou.

Line A follows the Shendan coast southward from the Barcelona terminal on the [[Península de la Barcelona]], through the western suburbs of Sant Cristòfor, the coastal municipalities of Cumará, and the canal corridor municipalities of Marjal del Canal. The line shares the Coastal Line tracks with [[Rodalies de Portnou]] Line 1, which provides local services within the Portnou metropolitan area.

== Route ==

=== Sant Cristòfor ===

Line A begins at [[Barcelona Main Station]] on the [[Península de la Barcelona]], the southern terminal serving the Barcelona [[Ciutats of Sant Cristòfor|ciutat]] and the surrounding western districts. From Barcelona, the line heads south through three stations in the [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]] ciutat — [[Dàrsena Nord]], [[Dàrsena Centre]], and [[Dàrsena Sud]] — serving the suburban middle-class western neighbourhoods of the district. The line then enters [[Mare de Déu del Mar (ciutat)|Mare de Déu del Mar]], the affluent beachfront ciutat, where it serves five stations: [[Mare de Déu del Mar (CristoCarril)|Mare de Déu del Mar]], [[Platja de Mare de Déu]], [[Els Pins]], [[La Calma]], and [[Mare de Déu Sud]]. The nine stations within Sant Cristòfor cover the western coastal suburbs of the city, serving both residential and beachfront communities.

=== Cumará ===

After leaving Sant Cristòfor, Line A enters the [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará comarca]], serving two municipalities along the coast. [[Costa Serena]] is a wealthy coastal exurb with gated communities and a private university, while [[Pla dels Horts, Cumará, Estret|Pla dels Horts]] is a semi-rural suburban municipality with scattered settlements. These stations provide commuter connections to Sant Cristòfor for the residents of the Cumará coast.

=== Marjal del Canal ===

The line enters the [[Marjal del Canal (comarca)|Marjal del Canal comarca]] at [[Sant Mateu, Marjal del Canal, Estret|Sant Mateu]], a commuter town near the Riu Burutí on the comarca's northern border. The next station is [[L'Encreuament, Marjal del Canal, Estret|L'Encreuament]], a railway junction where the Coastal Line and [[Portnou Line]] cross. In [[Les Drassanes]], Line A stops only at [[Aeroport de Portnou]] station, adjacent to the terminal at [[Portnou International Airport]]. The other stations in Les Drassanes — [[Drassanes Nord]] and [[Les Drassanes (CristoCarril)|Les Drassanes]] — are served by [[Rodalies de Portnou]] Line 1, which provides local services on the same Coastal Line tracks.

=== Portnou ===

After passing through Les Drassanes, Line A enters [[Portnou]], stopping at [[El Coll Oest]] in the northwestern neighbourhood of [[El Coll]] before terminating at the [[Estació Central de Portnou]], the city's principal rail hub. The stations between El Coll Oest and the Estació Central are served by Rodalies de Portnou Line 1.

