== Service pattern ==

Line A operates three service patterns between [[Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Portnou]]:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Service !! Stops !! Stations served !! Travel time
|-
| '''Short''' || All stops 1–9 || Barcelona Main Station to Mare de Déu Sud || ~35 min
|-
| '''Express''' || 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 14, 16 || Barcelona Main Station to Estació Central de Portnou, skipping intermediate stations || ~71 min
|-
| '''Local''' || All stops 1–16 || Barcelona Main Station to Estació Central de Portnou || ~85 min
|}

The '''short''' service operates entirely within [[Sant Cristòfor]], running from Barcelona Main Station through the western ciutats to Mare de Déu Sud. This is the most frequent service, providing high-capacity commuter rail for the suburban corridors of [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]] and [[Mare de Déu del Mar (ciutat)|Mare de Déu del Mar]].

The '''express''' service provides the fastest connection between Sant Cristòfor and Portnou, stopping at the first five stations in Sant Cristòfor before running non-stop to [[Aeroport de Portnou]] and the [[Estació Central de Portnou]]. The express skips all stations in [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará]] and the outer [[Marjal del Canal (comarca)|Marjal del Canal]] municipalities, reducing the end-to-end journey to approximately 71 minutes. The express is primarily used by airport passengers and long-distance commuters between the two cities.

The '''local''' service stops at all 16 stations along the full 83.3 km route, with an end-to-end journey time of approximately 85 minutes. The local provides the only CristoCarril service to the intermediate stations in Cumará (Costa Serena, Pla dels Horts) and the outer Marjal del Canal municipalities ([[Sant Mateu, Marjal del Canal, Estret|Sant Mateu]], [[L'Encreuament, Marjal del Canal, Estret|L'Encreuament]]). Within [[Les Drassanes]], the local stops only at [[Aeroport de Portnou]]; the stations [[Drassanes Nord]] and [[Les Drassanes (CristoCarril)|Les Drassanes]] are served by [[Rodalies de Portnou]] Line 1 on the same Coastal Line tracks. In the Portnou area, the local stops at [[El Coll Oest]] before terminating at the Estació Central de Portnou, with intermediate stations served by Rodalies Line 1.

== Schedule ==

Line A operates from approximately 5:00 AM to 12:30 AM daily. Frequencies vary by service pattern and time of day:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Service !! Peak (7–10 AM, 4–7 PM) !! Off-peak (daytime) !! Evening (after 8 PM) !! Weekend
|-
| '''Short''' || every 10 min || every 15 min || every 20 min || every 20 min (daytime), every 30 min (evening)
|-
| '''Express''' || every 20 min || every 30 min || every 60 min || every 30 min (daytime), every 60 min (evening)
|-
| '''Local''' || every 30 min || every 60 min || every 90 min || every 60 min (daytime), every 90 min (evening)
|}

The short service is the most frequent, reflecting the high commuter demand within the Sant Cristòfor western suburbs. The express provides a regular connection between the two cities and the airport, with reduced evening and weekend frequency. The local is the least frequent, reflecting the lower ridership at the intermediate stations in Cumará and outer Marjal del Canal. Combined, the three services provide up to 12 trains per hour on the inner section between Barcelona Main Station and Mare de Déu del Mar during peak periods.

== Fares ==

Line A uses the [[Tarifa Integrada]] zonal fare system, which is shared across the CristoCarril network and integrated with the [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Rodalies de Portnou]] systems. The line crosses four fare zones:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Zone !! Stations !! Fare (B$)
|-
| 1 || Barcelona Main Station to Dàrsena Sud (stations 1–4) || 2.50
|-
| 2 || Mare de Déu del Mar to Mare de Déu Sud (stations 5–9) || 3.75
|-
| 3 || Costa Serena to L'Encreuament (stations 10–13) || 5.25
|-
| 4 || Aeroport de Portnou to Estació Central de Portnou (stations 14–16) || 6.50
|}

Fares are calculated based on the number of zones travelled through. Passengers using a [[Tarifa Integrada]] smart card receive free transfers to connecting metro, streetcar, and Rodalies services within a 90-minute window. Concession fares (half price) are available to seniors, students, and children under 12. Children under 5 travel free. Monthly and weekly passes are available with discounts of up to 40% off the single-ride fare.

